 "notes": [
  "Measured: traced the provided developer plan; no photographs were supplied. Coordinates use x right, z down and metres.",
  "Printed: room 1 entrance hall 2.3 m2; room 2 living room 16.8 m2; room 3 bedroom 14.2 m2; room 4 bathroom 4.6 m2; room 5 balcony 3.4 m2; total 41.3 m2.",
  "Printed: living 5750 and 3350 mm; bedroom 5100 and 2750 mm; bathroom 2550 and 2100 mm; balcony 1000 and 3150 mm.",
  "Measured: scale about 57.3 pixels/m, cross-checked using bedroom 291px/5.10m, bedroom 158px/2.75m, living height 191px/3.35m, and bathroom 145px/2.55m. Raster edges carry several centimetres uncertainty.",
  "Derived: hall/living division is a floor zoning boundary only, with no separating wall. Bathroom and structural-column recesses follow the thick bands; thin dimension lines are not walls.",
  "Measured: balcony has a left-hand door from living and a bottom door from bedroom; the open outer edge is represented by a railing. Door and window widths span the complete drawn gaps.",
  "Assumed: 2.7 m ceiling, 2.05 m internal door heads, 2.5 m facade glazing heads with 0.1 m window sills. No photos are available to confirm heights, wall paint or flooring; neutral warm wall paint, timber-toned dry-room floors and grey wet-room tiles are placeholders.",
  "Derived: grey X rectangles are service shafts, outlined by wall bands rather than treated as furniture. The blue X beneath the bathroom column is interpreted as a washing machine; the larger upper-left bathroom zone with shower control is interpreted as a shower.",
  "Assumed: kitchen upper cupboards, extractor, fixture heights and appliance identities are inferred from the plan and standard construction; the balcony blue-X box is treated as an outdoor mechanical unit. No radiators are clearly drawn.",
  "Measured: the printed room table and rounded dimensions are retained verbatim; traced usable polygons include recesses and do not force agreement with rectangular dimension products."
 ],
